 "description": "# \n\nTask Description: Problem Statement There is an integer sequence A of length N whose values are unknown.\nGiven is an integer sequence B of length N-1 which is known to satisfy the following:\n B_i >= \\max(A_i, A_{i+1}) \nFind the maximum possible sum of the elements of A.\nTask Constraint: All values in input are integers.\n2 <= N <= 100\n0 <= B_i <= 10^5\nTask Input: Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nB_1 B_2 . . . B_{N-1}\nTask Output: Print the maximum possible sum of the elements of A.\nTask Samples: input: 3\n2 5 output: 9\n\nA can be, for example, ( 2 , 1 , 5 ), ( -1 , -2 , -3 ), or ( 2 , 2 , 5 ). Among those candidates, A = ( 2 , 2 , 5 ) has the maximum possible sum.\ninput: 2\n3 output: 6\ninput: 6\n0 153 10 10 23 output: 53\n\n## Constraints\nAll values in input are integers.\n2 <= N <= 100\n0 <= B_i <= 10^5\n\n## Input\nInput is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nB_1 B_2 . . . B_{N-1}\n\n## Output\nPrint the maximum possible sum of the elements of A.\n\n## Examples\n['input: 3\\n2 5 output: 9\\n\\nA can be, for example, ( 2 , 1 , 5 ), ( -1 , -2 , -3 ), or ( 2 , 2 , 5 ). Among those candidates, A = ( 2 , 2 , 5 ) has the maximum possible sum.', 'input: 2\\n3 output: 6', 'input: 6\\n0 153 10 10 23 output: 53']",
